WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:04.968
-It is Kate McKinnon!
That's exactly what you want.

00:00:04.968 --> 00:00:09.701
I am so happy you
have entered the building.

00:00:09.701 --> 00:00:11.133
-Okay, that was fun.
Thank you so much.

00:00:11.133 --> 00:00:12.267
-No, no, no, no. We have more.

00:00:12.267 --> 00:00:14.167
I didn't even
start a question yet.

00:00:14.167 --> 00:00:16.167
Kate, I have a lot to
talk to you about,

00:00:16.167 --> 00:00:18.634
because I got to see you
quickly in London.

00:00:18.634 --> 00:00:21.334
-Yes.
-We saw each other fast.

00:00:21.334 --> 00:00:22.934
-I was there.
-Yeah, you were in London.

00:00:22.934 --> 00:00:25.534
-I saw you and I left,
because why I would stay?

00:00:25.534 --> 00:00:28.067
-Yeah. What else does London
have to offer?

00:00:28.067 --> 00:00:30.534
-It's Fallon, baby. That's it.

00:00:30.534 --> 00:00:32.534
-But you brought a --
You brought a photo.

00:00:32.534 --> 00:00:35.234
And I got to be honest,
I knew what this was.

00:00:35.234 --> 00:00:38.434
-Oh, you did. So, I didn't.
So, I like to walk.

00:00:38.434 --> 00:00:40.267
I like to see stuff.

00:00:40.267 --> 00:00:42.000
And I saw -- Thank you.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:43.234
-Yeah.
-Thank you.

00:00:43.234 --> 00:00:44.501
-Amazing. We do, too.

00:00:44.501 --> 00:00:47.734
-It's important to get out there
and see what is up.

00:00:47.734 --> 00:00:50.267
So, I love bugs.

00:00:50.267 --> 00:00:52.701
And I saw this baby
on the street.

00:00:52.701 --> 00:00:55.400
And I was like, "Oh, my God."

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:57.868
This moth. What?

00:00:57.868 --> 00:01:03.634
It's, like, sepia-toned wing,
fishnets, basically.

00:01:03.634 --> 00:01:04.667
-Basically. It's gorgeous.

00:01:04.667 --> 00:01:06.801
-Peek of red with polka dots.

00:01:06.801 --> 00:01:09.000
Like, this is
a burlesque dancer.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:11.434
-Yeah, this is the most gorgeous
bug I've ever seen.

00:01:11.434 --> 00:01:13.701
-This moth has
tassels on her boobs

00:01:13.701 --> 00:01:15.200
and is ready to do a wig change.

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:18.534
-Yes.
-This is, like, a moth.

00:01:18.534 --> 00:01:19.567
-Yes.

00:01:19.567 --> 00:01:21.000
-And then I saw,
a few days later --

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:24.434
-This in "The New York Times."

00:01:24.434 --> 00:01:26.667
-You're supposed to --
-"Kill this bug."

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:30.501
Kill. They want you to kill
this -- murder this bug.

00:01:30.501 --> 00:01:34.467
-Kill with no mercy, they said.
Kill it with no mercy.

00:01:34.467 --> 00:01:36.033
-Spotted lantern fly.

00:01:36.033 --> 00:01:38.934
-Yeah, so, apparently, they're
an incredibly invasive pest,

00:01:38.934 --> 00:01:43.200
and you're supposed to
murder them on contact.

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:47.901
And I was, like,
"Um, yeah, okay, I will."

00:01:47.901 --> 00:01:49.133
-You were not.
-Because --

00:01:49.133 --> 00:01:50.868
-You were like,
"Where did I find that moth?"

00:01:50.868 --> 00:01:52.334
And you had to go back
to that location to --

00:01:52.334 --> 00:01:55.167
-The next one I see,
I'm going to be like, "Run!

00:01:55.167 --> 00:01:56.400
Run!"
-You are not.

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:58.601
-No, we're supposed to.
No, we're supposed to.

00:01:58.601 --> 00:01:59.934
We're supposed to, and I will.

00:01:59.934 --> 00:02:02.100
I will kill
the next lantern fly I see.

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:05.234
-But take a photo of it.
Oh, my God. You're winking.

00:02:05.234 --> 00:02:07.367
-No, we're supposed to.
I will.

00:02:07.367 --> 00:02:08.868
I will kill the next one.

00:02:08.868 --> 00:02:10.100
-Can I tell you what's
interesting right now?

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:11.901
-Uh-huh. Yeah, yeah.

00:02:11.901 --> 00:02:14.167
-I saw, last year on
"Saturday Night Live,"

00:02:14.167 --> 00:02:16.901
Chloe Fineman did
an impression of you to you.

00:02:16.901 --> 00:02:18.667
-Yeah.
-An impression of you to you.

00:02:18.667 --> 00:02:22.467
-She did. It was great.
-She kind of nailed it.

00:02:22.467 --> 00:02:24.133
This is a picture of --

00:02:24.133 --> 00:02:28.200
-I don't know what she's --
I don't sit like that.

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:29.767
-I mean, you kind of --

00:02:29.767 --> 00:02:32.601
-I don't -- I would never sit --
-You kind of sit like that.

00:02:32.601 --> 00:02:33.734
-How weird would that be

00:02:33.734 --> 00:02:36.434
if I just, like,
sat like that all the time?

00:02:36.434 --> 00:02:37.868
-You do kind of
sit like that, though.

00:02:37.868 --> 00:02:40.234
-Yeah, I do.

00:02:40.234 --> 00:02:41.734
-You announced earlier this year
that you're leaving

00:02:41.734 --> 00:02:43.067
"Saturday Night Live."

00:02:43.067 --> 00:02:45.033
-I did. You know, I left.
I left "Saturday Night Live."

00:02:45.033 --> 00:02:47.467
-You left it, bud.
But what a great run.

00:02:47.467 --> 00:02:48.901
-The love of my life.
-We're going to miss you.

00:02:48.901 --> 00:02:50.467
-"Saturday Night Live."
-Yeah.

00:02:50.467 --> 00:02:53.033
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thank you. Thanks.

00:02:53.033 --> 00:02:54.734
-We're going to miss you.
You were so great.

00:02:54.734 --> 00:02:57.100
-I'm going to miss it.

00:02:57.100 --> 00:03:00.367
-Did you clear out the office
and all that stuff?

00:03:00.367 --> 00:03:02.267
-I have not yet
cleared out my office,

00:03:02.267 --> 00:03:03.501
because there's just too much --

00:03:03.501 --> 00:03:06.567
There's like a decade
of junk in there.

00:03:06.567 --> 00:03:10.334
I think I'm going to leave
behind some surprises.

00:03:10.334 --> 00:03:11.467
-Yeah.
Which is nice of you to do.

00:03:11.467 --> 00:03:13.734
-Because I started collecting --

00:03:13.734 --> 00:03:16.334
You know, I had to play
Anthony Fauci a lot

00:03:16.334 --> 00:03:19.334
and some other people that
required the use of prosthetics.

00:03:19.334 --> 00:03:25.234
So I started, just for fun,
collecting the prosthetic items,

00:03:25.234 --> 00:03:27.167
the noses and ears
and things like that.

00:03:27.167 --> 00:03:31.400
And I started making little art
pieces with them in my office.

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:33.868
Like, I said to
a writer friend like,

00:03:33.868 --> 00:03:35.167
"Oh, come get your Gatorade.

00:03:35.167 --> 00:03:36.367
It's in my office."

00:03:36.367 --> 00:03:40.901
And then I sort of had done --
had made that.

00:03:40.901 --> 00:03:41.934
-Piece of art.

00:03:41.934 --> 00:03:43.901
-Just a bouquet of
noses and ears.

00:03:43.901 --> 00:03:44.968
-Yeah.

00:03:44.968 --> 00:03:46.634
-And then I said
to one of the writers,

00:03:46.634 --> 00:03:48.901
"Just go --
I left something on the piano.

00:03:48.901 --> 00:03:50.934
Can you go find it?"

00:03:50.934 --> 00:03:54.300
-I mean, that's all Fauci noses.
-And those are noses.

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:56.167
-They're noses, by the way.
-They're noses.

00:03:56.167 --> 00:03:58.734
-Just for -- Yeah.
Just for NBC censors.

00:03:58.734 --> 00:04:01.767
Yeah, that's what they are.
They're noses.

00:04:01.767 --> 00:04:06.434
But are you prepared for
a non-"SNL,"

00:04:06.434 --> 00:04:09.834
a year of not going into work
at 1:00 in the afternoon

00:04:09.834 --> 00:04:11.167
and staying up until
4:00 in the morning every night?

00:04:11.167 --> 00:04:12.868
-I'd like to --
I'd like to think I am.

00:04:12.868 --> 00:04:18.634
My cat has been like,
"Oh, now you're home.

00:04:18.634 --> 00:04:22.400
After a decade of you
being gone, out all hours,

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:23.467
now you're home.

00:04:23.467 --> 00:04:26.067
Fine.
Well, I'm already asleep."

00:04:27.334 --> 00:04:29.934
-"Well, I'm not --
Well, then fine.

00:04:29.934 --> 00:04:32.334
Then I'm going to sleep."
-"Well, now I'm staying up.

00:04:32.334 --> 00:04:35.167
I'll stay up all night,
and you won't know where I am.

00:04:35.167 --> 00:04:37.434
How about that?"

00:04:37.434 --> 00:04:40.133
-Was it fun for you to
do "DC League of Super-Pets?"

00:04:40.133 --> 00:04:41.267
-Oh, it was wonderful.
It was wonderful.

00:04:41.267 --> 00:04:43.801
-You were fantastically funny
in that.

00:04:43.801 --> 00:04:46.033
And I thought the idea
is actually brilliant,

00:04:46.033 --> 00:04:47.767
that superheroes
should have pets.

00:04:47.767 --> 00:04:50.434
-It's -- And the pets are
heroes, as well.

00:04:50.434 --> 00:04:52.467
-Yes! Wow! Remember that.

00:04:52.467 --> 00:04:54.400
-The more you know.
-The more you know, yeah.

00:04:54.400 --> 00:04:56.000
-Yeah.
-This is who you play.

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:57.300
Is that the cutest thing
you've ever seen?

00:04:57.300 --> 00:05:00.567
-Yeah, so, that's Lulu.
She's the evil guinea pig.

00:05:00.567 --> 00:05:02.234
-Star of the movie. Oh, my gosh.

00:05:02.234 --> 00:05:03.501
You were the villain
of the movie.

00:05:03.501 --> 00:05:05.400
-Yes, yes. But it's still --

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:08.200
-The cutest thing
you've ever seen and so funny.

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:09.501
-How bad could that be?

00:05:09.501 --> 00:05:13.033
-But you are actually
a guinea pig who Lex Luthor

00:05:13.033 --> 00:05:18.167
has tested chemicals and stuff
and superpowers on Lulu.

00:05:18.167 --> 00:05:20.300
-Yes, and now she's got
an ax to grind.

00:05:20.300 --> 00:05:21.467
-That's exactly right. Yeah.

00:05:21.467 --> 00:05:23.501
So, finally,
the guinea pig is getting back

00:05:23.501 --> 00:05:25.200
and saying,
"Yeah, don't test stuff on me."

00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:26.334
-But this is -- To me, this is

00:05:26.334 --> 00:05:27.767
the essence of
a comedic character,

00:05:27.767 --> 00:05:29.133
an evil guinea pig.

00:05:29.133 --> 00:05:34.200
-You got giant laughs from
7-year-olds to 47-year-old.

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:36.200
-Well, that makes me so happy.
Thanks.

00:05:36.200 --> 00:05:38.067
-You got -- I wish --
-That makes me happy.

00:05:38.067 --> 00:05:39.701
-I wish --
If I had your number, I --

00:05:39.701 --> 00:05:41.801
I just wanted to, like, play it,
because you were crushing it.

00:05:41.801 --> 00:05:43.467
-Oh, that's really nice.
-Yeah.

00:05:43.467 --> 00:05:44.834
And you weren't even there,
but it was --

00:05:44.834 --> 00:05:46.834
You crushed it, and you have to
feel good about this.

00:05:46.834 --> 00:05:48.167
You made a lot of people happy.
-Thanks.

00:05:48.167 --> 00:05:49.467
-I want to show everyone a clip.

00:05:49.467 --> 00:05:52.434
Here's Kate McKinnon in
"DC League of Super-Pets."

00:05:52.434 --> 00:05:53.434
Take a look at this.

00:05:53.434 --> 00:05:55.534
-The dog is right.

00:05:55.534 --> 00:05:57.834
He should seek his freedom.

00:05:57.834 --> 00:05:59.767
-You see that? Lulu gets it.

00:05:59.767 --> 00:06:03.267
-And he must destroy all
who stand in his way.

00:06:03.267 --> 00:06:04.267
[ Cage creaking ]

00:06:04.267 --> 00:06:06.834
-Wow. That just took a turn.

00:06:06.834 --> 00:06:09.400
-You may kid yourself
with your silly fun,

00:06:09.400 --> 00:06:13.434
but I have the device!

00:06:13.434 --> 00:06:16.334
For one day soon,
when the stars align,

00:06:16.334 --> 00:06:20.067
the device will bring me
ultimate power and I will be...

00:06:20.067 --> 00:06:22.901
-You'll be more than free.
-...more than free.

00:06:22.901 --> 00:06:24.067
Exactly.

00:06:24.067 --> 00:06:26.367
-Lulu, whatever they
tested on you in that lab

00:06:26.367 --> 00:06:28.467
left you a few guineas
short of a pig.

00:06:28.467 --> 00:06:31.434
That device is just
a pile of garbage.

00:06:31.434 --> 00:06:33.334
-You fear my brilliance.
[ Chuckles ]

00:06:33.334 --> 00:06:35.901
Recede into shadows.
Recede into shadows.

00:06:35.901 --> 00:06:37.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:40.300 --> 00:06:41.634
-Kate McKinnon, everybody!

00:06:41.634 --> 00:06:45.801
"DC League of Super-Pets"
is in theaters now.

00:06:45.801 --> 00:06:47.601
We'll be right back with
Lili Reinhart.

00:06:47.601 --> 00:06:48.634
Stick around, everybody.

